00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:56,000
Richard Pryor: Live on the Sunset Strip is a comedy,
documentary film directed by Joe Layton.

2
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Richard Pryor's stand-up act includes his frank discussion about his freebasing
addiction, as well as the infamous night on June 9, 1980 that he caught on fire.

3
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Self, played by Richard Pryor.

4
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:26,000
Stoned Hippie (uncredited), played by Gene Cross.

5
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:16,000
Self - Audience Member (uncredited), played by Julie Hampton.

6
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:06,000
Self - Audience Member (uncredited), played by Jesse Jackson.

7
00:47:50,000 --> 00:47:56,000
Richard Pryor: Live on the Sunset Strip is the seventeenth
album by American comedian Richard Pryor.

8
00:54:40,000 --> 00:54:46,000
Produced by Pryor and Biff Dawes, the album was released
alongside the comedian's film of the same name in 1982.

9
01:01:30,000 --> 01:01:36,000
The material includes Pryor's frank discussion of his drug addiction and of the
night that he caught on fire while freebasing cocaine in 1980.

10
01:08:20,000 --> 01:08:26,000
The album later won the Grammy Award for Best Comedy Recording in 1982.

11
01:15:10,000 --> 01:15:16,000
The tone is lighthearted.
